REM Protects the IOLIST statement: standalone, behind a numeric label, an ordinary named
REM label and a label named with the word `label`, with an item list mixing a numeric
REM scalar, a string variable and an all-elements array subscript, a long item list spread
REM over a continuation line, upper-, lower- and mixed-case spellings, and a channel-option
REM reference to the leading label of an IOLIST statement.
IOLIST NUM1,STR1$,ARR1[ALL]
L10: iolist NUM2,STR2$
recio: IOLIST NUM3,STR3$
label: iolist NUM4,STR4$
IOLIST I1,I2,I3,I4,I5,I6,I7,I8,
:I9,I10
iolist NUM5,STR5$
IoList NUM6,STR6$
chanio: iolist CHNUM,CHSTR$
READ(1)IOL=CHANIO
